FORMAT: 1A
HOST: https://api.example.com

# Bookstore API

A typical everyday API Blueprint service: a books collection with create and
list actions, an item resource with URI parameters, and MSON data structures
for the request and response payloads.

## Books Collection [/books]

### List all books [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (array[Book])

### Add a book [POST]

+ Request (application/json)
    + Attributes (NewBook)

+ Response 201 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Book)

## Book [/books/{id}]

+ Parameters
    + id (string, required) - Unique book identifier.

### Get a book [GET]

+ Response 200 (application/json)
    + Attributes (Book)

+ Response 404

### Remove a book [DELETE]

+ Response 204

# Data Structures

## Book (object)
+ id: `b-42` (string, required) - Unique book identifier.
+ title: `The Left Hand of Darkness` (string, required) - Book title.
+ author: `Ursula K. Le Guin` (string, required) - Author name.
+ price: 9.99 (number, required) - Retail price.
+ inStock: true (boolean) - Whether the book is currently stocked.

## NewBook (object)
+ title: `The Left Hand of Darkness` (string, required) - Book title.
+ author: `Ursula K. Le Guin` (string, required) - Author name.
+ price: 9.99 (number, required) - Retail price.
